# 7. What is a port?

An IP address identifies a machine.

A **port** identifies a particular network service on that machine.

Think of an apartment building:

```text
IP address = building
Port = apartment
```

For example:

```text
193.40.157.25:11722
```

means:

```text
machine = 193.40.157.25
service entry point = 11722
```

SSH normally uses port 22, but your course VM uses a different externally exposed port.

Nginx normally uses:

```text
port 80
```

So you can have:

```text
193.40.157.25:11722
        │
        └── SSH

VM:80
  │
  └── Nginx / HTTP
```

