# 8. SSH authentication: passwords vs keys

SSH can authenticate you using a password or cryptographic keys.

Your course uses **SSH key authentication**.

You have two related files:

```text
~/.ssh/id_ed25519
~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
```

The important distinction:

```text
id_ed25519
    ↓
PRIVATE KEY
KEEP SECRET

id_ed25519.pub
    ↓
PUBLIC KEY
Can be shared
```

Think of it like:

```text
Private key = your secret physical key

Public key = the lock that recognizes that key
```

The public key can be placed on a server.

The private key stays on your control machine.

