# 46. SSH host key problem

You encountered:

```text
REMOTE HOST IDENTIFICATION HAS CHANGED!
```

SSH stores server identity information in:

```text
~/.ssh/known_hosts
```

SSH uses this to protect against connecting to an unexpected server.

You resolved it with:

```bash
ssh-keygen -f ~/.ssh/known_hosts -R '[193.40.157.25]:11722'
```

This removes the old stored host key for that address/port.

Important distinction:

```text
known_hosts
    ↓
identifies REMOTE SERVERS
```

while:

```text
id_ed25519
    ↓
identifies YOU
```

They're completely different things.

