# 102. And the Ansible syntax pattern

Ansible YAML follows another pattern:

```yaml
- name: Human-readable task name
  module:
    parameter: value
    parameter: value
```

For example:

```yaml
- name: Install Nginx
  ansible.builtin.apt:
    name: nginx
    state: present
```

Think:

```text
TASK
 │
 ├── name
 │
 └── MODULE
      │
      ├── parameter
      └── parameter
```

A play:

```yaml
- name: Web servers
  hosts: web_servers
  roles:
    - nginx
```

Think:

```text
PLAY
 │
 ├── name
 ├── hosts
 └── roles
      └── nginx
```

An inventory:

```ini
hostname ansible_host=IP ansible_port=PORT ansible_user=USER

[group]
hostname
```

Think:

```text
HOST DEFINITION
      +
GROUP MEMBERSHIP
```

